# Parquet is internally compressed, so git cannot delta successive versions —
# every ETL run stores 10-25 MB of fresh whole blobs. Tracking the tables in LFS
# keeps that churn out of the pack. Existing blobs stay in history; this only
# stops the growth.
#
# CI must fetch them, because actions/checkout does NOT pull LFS objects by
# default. Without them the build sees pointer files and Store() fails (with the
# message it raises for exactly this case). .github/workflows/pages.yml does NOT
# use checkout's `lfs: true` — it caches .git/lfs keyed on a hash of the pointer
# files and runs `git lfs pull` only on a miss, so unchanged tables cost no LFS
# bandwidth. Leaving checkout at lfs: false is load-bearing there: the pointer
# files on disk are what the cache key hashes.
data/parquet/*.parquet filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
